WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.001
Did you know?

2
00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:03.621
High blood pressure is a silent risk.

3
00:00:03.621 --> 00:00:09.500
And if you have a Black African or Black Caribbean background, your risk is higher.

4
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.912
It doesn't usually cause symptoms.

5
00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:16.440
As many as five million adults in the UK may have it without knowing.

6
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.000
The only way to know is to get checked.

7
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:28.000
Left untreated, it raises your risk of heart attack, heart disease, heart failure, stroke, kidney disease and vascular dementia.

8
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.303
Small swaps help.

9
00:00:29.303 --> 00:00:34.717
Adults should have no more than six grams of salt a day, about one level teaspoon.

10
00:00:34.717 --> 00:00:35.906
Using stock cubes?

11
00:00:35.906 --> 00:00:40.000
Pick ones that are lower in salt, and go easy on salty sauces.

12
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.709
A reading of one hundred and forty over ninety or higher is high.

13
00:00:44.709 --> 00:00:49.865
Many pharmacies offer free checks if you're forty or over, or ask your GP.

14
00:00:49.865 --> 00:00:51.676
Not checked in five years?

15
00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:53.000
Book one this week.

16
00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.358
When did you last check yours?

17
00:00:55.358 --> 00:01:03.200
Tell us below, and apply to join the Igbo Healthcare Professionals Network, IHPN-UK, at the link in our bio.
